WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.642 --> 00:00:15.962
stared at the diner entrance.

2
00:00:17.203 --> 00:00:19.544
"Why are humans so complicated?"

3
00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:20.404
she thought.

4
00:00:20.424 --> 00:00:27.188
"If they could read minds like Astralians, I wouldn't have to explain things to Bethany—she'd already know the

5
00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:33.233
truth!" "What's the matter, hon?"

6
00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:34.314
Flo asked.

7
00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.556
"Is something bothering you?"

8
00:00:36.576 --> 00:00:37.957
"There is.

9
00:00:37.977 --> 00:00:41.500
I—" "Tonight's going to be epic!"

10
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.902
Barry cried, bursting into the diner.

11
00:00:45.203 --> 00:00:46.324
Ally scowled at him.

12
00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:50.888
"I know you wanted to try out the plate levitation trick tonight, Barry.

13
00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:53.249
But please don't.

14
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.752
This night is too important to Ray."

15
00:00:56.692 --> 00:00:57.853
Barry gave her a thumbs-up.

16
00:00:57.873 --> 00:00:58.734
"Got it."

17
00:00:58.754 --> 00:01:01.876
"Go on, Ally," Flo said.

18
00:01:01.896 --> 00:01:03.578
"What were you saying?"

19
00:01:04.478 --> 00:01:09.081
Ally didn't want to talk about her problems in front of Barry, but she needed advice about Bethany.

20
00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:10.542
"I know!

21
00:01:10.922 --> 00:01:11.903
I'll ask Alpha!"

22
00:01:12.343 --> 00:01:12.844
Ally thought.

23
00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:16.106
"It's nothing, Flo, thanks," Ally said.

24
00:01:16.126 --> 00:01:19.288
"I'm going to fix my hair before the gala begins."

25
00:01:23.991 --> 00:01:26.773
Ally ducked into the restroom and reached into her apron pocket.

26
00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:28.454
But Alpha wasn't there!

27
00:01:30.155 --> 00:01:31.076
Ally checked everywhere.

28
00:01:32.468 --> 00:01:35.030
She checked the floor under the sink and next to the toilet.

29
00:01:36.451 --> 00:01:37.292
Alpha was gone.

30
00:01:37.913 --> 00:01:40.575
Again! "Maybe I dropped her in the dining room!"

31
00:01:41.115 --> 00:01:43.337
Ally raced out of the restroom to search for Alpha.

32
00:01:43.677 --> 00:01:45.959
But the gala guests had begun to arrive.

33
00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.442
There was no way Ally could search for Alpha now.

34
00:01:49.462 --> 00:01:54.746
"I can't even listen for Alpha's strange noises because I powered her down," she thought.

35
00:01:54.766 --> 00:01:55.847
"Now what?"

36
00:01:56.928 --> 00:02:01.492
"Ally!" Randy waved her into the kitchen and handed her a tray of appetizers.

37
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.661
"Pass around these Cosmic Crescents.

38
00:02:05.102 --> 00:02:08.044
They're puff pastry filled with spinach and cheese."

39
00:02:08.744 --> 00:02:12.607
Ally knew the gala was very important to Ray; it needed to go perfectly.

40
00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.669
But she was having a hard time keeping her mind on her job.

41
00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.813
As she wound her way through the guests, passing out food, she sneaked peeks under tables and in

42
00:02:21.873 --> 00:02:26.956
corners. "Alpha has to be somewhere in the diner," Ally thought.

43
00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:32.220
Once the tray of Cosmic Crescents was empty, Ally went back to the kitchen for another tray.

44
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.262
"These are Spinning Suns," Randy said.

45
00:02:36.282 --> 00:02:39.444
"They're mini pizzas with cheese and yellow peppers.

46
00:02:40.264 --> 00:02:42.845
Please tell people to be careful—they're hot."

47
00:02:45.407 --> 00:02:49.829
Ally had just begun to pass out the Spinning Suns when something underneath a table caught her eye.

48
00:02:50.389 --> 00:02:52.991
It was small and shiny—just like the device!

49
00:02:54.792 --> 00:02:57.433
Still holding the tray, Ally rushed across the diner.

50
00:02:57.753 --> 00:03:01.736
But she was so focused on the object under the table, she wasn't looking where she was going.

51
00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:08.342
Boom! She slammed into a tall gentleman who'd just entered the diner, and the tray of hot Spinning

52
00:03:08.402 --> 00:03:09.642
Suns flew out of her hand.

53
00:03:10.002 --> 00:03:14.564
Ally quickly activated her levitation powers and stopped the tray just before it hit the floor.

54
00:03:15.224 --> 00:03:16.585
She grabbed the tray and turned to him.

55
00:03:16.605 --> 00:03:17.925
"Sorry, sir.

56
00:03:17.945 --> 00:03:19.305
I didn't see you there."

57
00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:20.986
The man smiled.

58
00:03:21.006 --> 00:03:23.507
"That was amazing, young lady!

59
00:03:23.527 --> 00:03:26.708
I've heard such wonderful things about your tricks.

60
00:03:27.508 --> 00:03:32.971
So when the League of Rocket Scientists invited me to be their keynote speaker, I knew I had

61
00:03:33.031 --> 00:03:33.871
to come tonight."

62
00:03:33.891 --> 00:03:38.393
"He's the president!"

63
00:03:38.793 --> 00:03:40.354
Ally thought as the man walked away.

64
00:03:40.374 --> 00:03:43.375
"And that was a close call!"

65
00:03:44.656 --> 00:03:47.197
She quickly glanced under the table to look for Alpha.

66
00:03:48.517 --> 00:03:49.898
"Ugh," she thought.

67
00:03:50.598 --> 00:03:53.620
The shiny object was someone's phone, not the device.

68
00:03:55.748 --> 00:04:00.430
While the guests ate and the president gave his speech, Ally took every chance she had to look

69
00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:00.970
for Alpha.

70
00:04:02.311 --> 00:04:06.893
"I can't believe I lost her a second time," Ally scolded herself.

71
00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:11.655
"I'm glad my parents aren't here—they'd be so disappointed in me."

72
00:04:11.675 --> 00:04:17.098
"Ally, it's almost time to present Randy's rocket ship cake," Flo said.

73
00:04:17.118 --> 00:04:21.240
"As soon as the president finishes his speech, you can carry it out."

74
00:04:24.128 --> 00:04:29.091
Ally went into the kitchen to get the cake, but Barry was already carrying the elaborately decorated cake.

75
00:04:29.111 --> 00:04:32.633
"Be careful," Ally warned.

76
00:04:32.653 --> 00:04:34.674
"No tricks."

77
00:04:34.694 --> 00:04:37.876
"Don't worry," Barry said.

78
00:04:37.896 --> 00:04:40.117
"This is going to be perfect!"

79
00:04:41.017 --> 00:04:46.000
As soon as Barry stepped into the dining room with the rocket ship cake, the guests exploded into

80
00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:50.823
applause. "That looks so real," one said.

81
00:04:50.843 --> 00:04:53.024
"I can't believe we can eat that!"

82
00:04:53.532 --> 00:04:54.133
another said.

83
00:04:54.773 --> 00:04:58.536
Ally held her breath as Barry made it all the way across the dining room with the cake.

84
00:04:59.116 --> 00:05:02.619
He was just about to set it down in front of the president when he tripped.

85
00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:07.062
The cake flew up—and landed right in the president's lap!

86
00:05:08.243 --> 00:05:13.727
The room went silent as Barry stood there looking shocked, a broken spring dangling from his finger.
